Cole Kitchen

KNOWN PROBLEMS:
My program passes all of the autograder tests, however I used integers to do my 
CV queue, so if you called wait on more than 1 billion threads, it would not be able to signal
any more than 1 billion. If I were to do the project again I would probably start with a linked list
and actually create a data structure for the CV tracking.

DESIGN:
I decided to use an array for my implementation of the project because I thought it would be faster.
I found out that it is actually not much faster than doing a linked list, and it also seems a bit cluttered
because I do keep track of two indexes and the number of threads, as well as a bunch of little flags
for multiple operations like join and the CVS and locks. I also thought it would save memory to not create
an actual queue for each CV, so I decided to use integers to essentially make a queue. This has a limitation
though because if you have 1 billion and 1 threads waiting, the last thread will never be able to be signaled.
The lowest order number it checks for is 1 billion, so anything past that it just wont see. This could
probably be fixed if you shifted all of the order numbers down by 1 when you take one off but it would 
require an extra loop, but I have not tried it out so maybe it could fit in the current for loop.

